   "text": {
    "L1": "Families come in many forms, and every caring family can support its members.",
    "L2": "Family members care for children and elders, share work and money, and pass on values, skills and stories.",
    "L3": "Housework is not one person's job. Everyone should help according to age and ability.",
    "L4": "For example, adults may cook, a Class 6 child may lay the table and fold clothes, and a young child may water plants.",
    "L5": "Tasks should be shared fairly, and disliked tasks can be rotated so nobody does everything.",
    "L6": "A community is larger than a family: neighbours or villagers can share work and help one another.",
    "L7": "When families and communities care together, support reaches more people."
   },
